# MVC-Based User Registration Web Application

A Java web application built using the MVC (Model-View-Controller) architecture pattern. The application allows users to submit a registration form through a JSP-based UI. User data is processed through Controller and Service layers and stored in an in-memory repository implemented using the DAO (Data Access Object) pattern with an ArrayList.

## Features

* MVC Architecture Implementation
* Layered Design (Controller, Service, Repository, Domain)
* DAO Pattern for Data Access
* JSP-based User Interface
* User Registration Form
* Form Validation and Submission Handling
* Success Message after Registration
* In-Memory Data Storage using ArrayList

## Architecture

* Controller Layer: Handles HTTP requests and responses.
* Service Layer: Contains business logic.
* Domain Layer: Represents user entities.
* Repository Layer: Manages data storage.
* DAO Layer: Provides abstraction for data access operations.
* JSP Views: Responsible for user interaction and presentation.

## Application Flow

1. User accesses the registration URL.
2. User fills out and submits the registration form.
3. Controller receives the request.
4. Service layer processes the data.
5. DAO saves the User object into an ArrayList repository.
6. Upon successful registration, a success message is displayed to the user.
7. Stored user data can be retrieved through repository methods.

## Technologies Used

* Java
* Servlets
* JSP
* MVC Architecture
* DAO Design Pattern
* Collections Framework (ArrayList)
* Apache Tomcat
